[9.135, "o", "miu-cr: 04:05:21.077 done: 1 findings\r\n\u001b[34m\u001b[1m● LOW (testing)\u001b[0m  \u001b[36minternal/engine/agent/prompt.go:35\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "    This sentence is the PR's entire behavioral change, yet no test references it, so an accidental revert of either copy (line 35 in `systemPrompt`, line 93 in `systemPromptXML`) would pass CI silently. The package convention pins significant prompt rules with `contains` assertions, as `TestSystemPromptPriorityRubric` does for the adjacent `reserve P0/P1 for issues that must block merge` rule and `TestSystemPromptDescribesSymbolContextRelations` does across both format variants. Add a `contains` pin for the new threshold line to both variants (fix belongs in `prompt_test.go`, not in this quoted line).\r\n  \u001b[2mcode:\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m│ - Report low and medium defects, not only merge blockers. Omit a note only when it is a style nit, or when the rationale would say the behavior is acceptable, by design, or \"no bug\".\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "1 finding(s):\r\n  low      1\r\n"]
[6.013, "o", "\u001b[2m# add --post with GITHUB_TOKEN to publish inline comments and one summary\u001b[0m\r\n"]
